WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.800
When you spin up a Jetpack Compose project, it hands you a pre-configured design architecture.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:13.600
The material theme object automatically cascades color roles, typography, and shape tokens down your entire component tree.

3
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.600
When the device shifts from light to dark, the framework handles the inversion natively.

4
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:23.200
React Native takes the opposite approach. It ships completely un-styled.

5
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.600
Because React Native provides raw UI primitives rather than an integrated design system,

6
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.200
building a scalable token-based architecture requires explicit setup.

7
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.600
You have to construct the structural plumbing that Compose provides by default.

8
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.800
Large production code bases typically solve this through one of two approaches.

9
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.600
Teams either roll a bespoke custom token system managed via React context,

10
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:52.400
or they adopt React Native paper, a third-party library that implements Material Design 3.

11
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.800
While the starting points differ, the underlying mechanics are highly compatible.

12
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:04.800
Both frameworks rely on declarative UI logic, meaning the way data flows through the component tree to trigger visual updates

13
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.400
follows the same structural patterns.

14
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:13.000
Migrating from Android to React Native does not require abandoning token-based design.

15
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.600
It simply requires you to manually define the theme architecture that you are used to receiving as a built-in feature.

16
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.200
To map this out, we will start at the OS hardware level.

17
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.800
Trace the two distinct React Native architectural paths,

18
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:33.600
and conclude with a definitive framework translation matrix, mapping Compose functions to React Native equivalents.

19
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:42.200
Achieving parity between these environments relies on recognizing that declarative UI systems share a common logic for state and styling,

20
00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.000
regardless of the specific API names.

21
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.200
Any dynamic declarative theme must originate from a hardware level signal provided by the operating system

22
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.600
to determine the baseline, light, or dark mode state.

23
00:01:54.600 --> 00:02:00.200
In Compose, you capture this hardware signal using is system and dark theme using.

24
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:05.600
In React Native, the use color scheme hook pushes the Boolean into your theme architecture.

25
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.000
The implementation follows two paths.

26
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:14.400
The first is a custom theme system, passing token definitions through create context down the component tree.

27
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:20.400
Teams use this custom context approach because it mirrors the logical token structure of Compose's material theme,

28
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.600
but allows the UI to deviate from material design visual guidelines.

29
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.000
The second path is React Native paper.

30
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.600
This acts as the direct equivalent to Compose's material theme.

31
00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:35.600
For strict material three parity, developers wrap their root app in a paper provider.

32
00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:41.800
To populate that provider, developers use Google's material theme builder to generate exact MD3 values,

33
00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.600
export them as JSON, and pass them into the paper configuration.

34
00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.000
Your choice is based on the specific design requirements of the product.

35
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.800
You either build bespoke architectural control via context,

36
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:58.000
or you achieve immediate framework parity by importing paper.

37
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.400
Moving from macro architecture down to implementation,

38
00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:07.000
requires translating abstract semantic tokens into explicit layout values.

39
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:14.800
Compose's material theme.typography scale maps directly to explicitly defined text variance in React Native paper,

40
00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.200
or to custom text components in a context system.

41
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.200
Shape tokens require literal translation.

42
00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.800
This table maps Compose's semantic shapes to React Native border radius integers.

43
00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.400
Shapes.extra small maps to 4, cascading down to 28 for extra large.

44
00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:38.400
To mimic shapes.full, assign a massive border radius of 1000 for the pill effect.

45
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:45.800
Defining these integer equivalent centrally in a token file ensures visual consistency across your React Native component tree,

46
00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.000
matching the exact result from composes shape tokens.

47
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.400
Replicating Android 12's Monet system, where the UI pulls color palettes from the user's wallpaper,

48
00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.800
introduces a technical hurdle for cross-platform apps.

49
00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:03.200
Compose handles Monet natively via dynamic dark color scheme.

50
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.000
Because React Native executes in JavaScript,

51
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.400
it cannot read these native OS tokens without a bridge.

52
00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:15.000
To access these colors, you either utilize a dedicated package like Expo Material 3 theme,

53
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:20.800
or write a custom turbo module to surface those native Android APIs to your JavaScript runtime.

54
00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.800
Once your colors are accessible, you must address a common architectural issue

55
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.200
that occurs when using both navigation and UI libraries.

56
00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.600
If you combine React Native paper with React navigation, they spin up independent theme states.

57
00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:38.800
This fragmented UI renders navigation headers in one color and the screen body in another.

58
00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.800
The solution is merging the navigation container theme with the paper provider theme at the root.

59
00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:48.000
Explicit synchronization between these core libraries is the only way

60
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.400
to ensure background and surface colors remain perfectly consistent across your React Native app.

61
00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:59.000
Moving between Jetpack Compose and React Native is less about learning a new UI philosophy

62
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.000
and more about translating identical logic between different APIs.

63
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.000
This translation matrix proves the logic matrix.

64
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.000
State memory remains consistent.

65
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.800
Compose's mutable state of maps to React Native's use state,

66
00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.400
while a basic remember maps to use ref.

67
00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.800
Launched effect logic translates directly to use effect dependency arrays.

68
00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:24.800
For layout, column, row, and box structures become view components organized by Flexbox rules.

69
00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:29.800
Architectural scopes like Composition local perform the same role as React context

70
00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:35.400
and the styling provided by Compose modifiers is handled by passing style objects into the style prop.

71
00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:42.000
Even your nav controller logic transfers smoothly over to standard use navigation hooks

72
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.200
inside a configured navigation container.

73
00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:49.000
Once you have mapped these declarative structural equivalents,

74
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:52.200
the friction of UI development decreases.

75
00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:56.400
This allows you to focus your attention on the deeper performance layer,

76
00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:01.400
the mechanics of the new architecture, Hermes, and Kotlin turbo modules.

